Z||000000||oneof547||12-04-2001||08:17 PM||||Howdy,<P>During a routine check of engine fluids, I discovered a trail of engine oil coming from the valve cover bolts or from right around the heads of these bolts. I ran the engine up to normal temperature and with the engine running, visually inspected this area and determined that for sure that it was coming from 2 of the bolts heads.  Is this a definite sign that my valve cover gasket needs to be replaced????? Is there another fix for this problem like RTV or additive???<P>            Thanks for your time!<P>                  oneof547<BR>             88 formula t-tops<p>[This message has been edited by oneof547 (edited 12-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||2birds||12-04-2001||10:01 PM||||Valve cover gaskets can be changed on the 2.8 without removing the upper and middle portions of the intake.  You just have to bend/remove the engine lifting brackets and undo the dogbone bracket for clearance.<BR>Fel-Pro makes a good set for about $20, and it comes with the RTV for the manifold-head junction.  The covers bolts have torque specs, too.  <BR>I'd also make sure it isn't the intake manifold end seals (possible) or the distributor O-ring (VERY probable if it has any mileage on it) that is another source of an oil leak.||||reg||1
